From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 11:13:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Ring render doorbells once per four
 renders by default

Measured on experimental 1.1093, one boot, four blocks alternating the
word at 0 and at 4: render.light at depth 1 170.35 against 170.45 us,
depth 8 59.75 against 62.95 us (-5.1 %), depth 64 59.25 against
61.30 us (-3.3 %); fill 1080p -0.1 % and geometry 1440p -0.7 %. The
stress pair passed and the pixel check gave one readback hash in every
block, no fault line appeared, and at depth 64 74 % of the render
publications were deferred, 0.52 doorbells per render (one ring of
both pipes per 3.8 renders). A group of 2, macOS's own rate of one
doorbell per render, read -0.90 us at depth 8 and at depth 64 on the
same kernel.

Set g16_render_bell_group to 4 by default. A render publication made
while at least four renders are in flight posts its records without
ringing, and the fourth such publication rings both pipes for all of
them; fewer in flight, or the end of a publish pass with fewer than four
in flight, rings as before. Nothing is allocated.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
index 51add7ea61..101816bfa7 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
@@ -2366,14 +2366,14 @@ pub(crate) fn pass_loop() -> u32 {
     "G16: extra retire and publish rounds a poll pass runs for firmware events that arrived during it, instead of waiting for the next pass (default 0: none; 1..4; runtime 0644)"
 );
 
-/// Storage of `g16_render_bell_group` (runtime 0644, default 0).
-static RENDER_BELL_GROUP: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(0);
+/// Storage of `g16_render_bell_group` (runtime 0644, default 4).
+static RENDER_BELL_GROUP: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(4);
 
 /// `g16_render_bell_group` k (2 to 16): a render publication made while at least k renders are
 /// already in flight posts its TA and FS records without ringing; the k-th such publication
 /// rings both pipes for all of them, so one firmware scheduler call takes the group. Owed
 /// records are rung at the end of any publish pass that finds fewer than k renders in flight
-/// (bell_group.rs). 0 (default) or any other value: every render publication rings, as before.
+/// (bell_group.rs). Default 4. 0 or any other value: every render publication rings, as before.
 /// Read at each render publication and publish pass.
 pub(crate) fn render_bell_group() -> u32 {
     RENDER_BELL_GROUP.load(Ordering::Relaxed)
@@ -2385,7 +2385,7 @@ pub(crate) fn render_bell_group() -> u32 {
     RENDER_BELL_GROUP_PARM,
     RENDER_BELL_GROUP,
     "g16_render_bell_group",
-    "G16: k = renders behind k others ring once per k publications (2-16; default 0, off)"
+    "G16: k = renders behind k others ring once per k publications (2-16; default 4; 0 = off)"
 );
 
 /// Storage of `g16_window_poll_us` (runtime 0644, default 0).
